{"id":16403,"date":"2026-06-29T05:55:46","date_gmt":"2026-06-29T05:55:46","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/?p=16403"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:21:31","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:21:31","slug":"whole-home-evaluation-before-remodeling","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/whole-home-evaluation-before-remodeling\/","title":{"rendered":"Why Every Remodeling Project Should Begin with a Whole Home Evaluation"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most homeowners begin planning a renovation with a single room in mind. It might be an outdated kitchen, a bathroom that no longer meets the family&#8217;s needs, or a living area that feels disconnected from the rest of the house. While focusing on one space is completely natural, it can sometimes limit the overall success of a remodeling project. Improvements made in isolation may solve one problem while unintentionally creating another somewhere else in the home. That is why Harris &amp; Sons believes every successful renovation should begin with something much broader\u2014a whole home evaluation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A whole home evaluation is more than a simple walkthrough or inspection. It is a comprehensive assessment of how every major system, structural component, and living space works together. Instead of concentrating only on the room scheduled for renovation, Harris &amp; Sons studies how the entire property functions as a complete environment. They examine structural conditions, circulation patterns, natural lighting, ventilation, plumbing, electrical systems, insulation, moisture control, and the way the family actually lives within the space. This broader understanding allows the team to identify opportunities that may otherwise remain hidden until construction is already underway.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Beginning with this larger perspective benefits homeowners in countless ways. It reduces the likelihood of expensive surprises, creates more realistic budgets, improves construction sequencing, and often uncovers simple solutions that deliver greater long-term value than originally expected. More importantly, it allows Harris &amp; Sons to design renovations that strengthen the entire home rather than simply updating one portion of it. The result is a remodeling experience built on confidence instead of guesswork.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">A Whole Home Evaluation Creates Better Remodeling Decisions<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Many renovation projects begin with a list of visible improvements. Homeowners often want new cabinetry, updated flooring, modern fixtures, or a more contemporary layout. Although these requests are important, they represent only one layer of the home&#8217;s overall condition. Before recommending any design solution, Harris &amp; Sons first seeks to understand why the existing space no longer works. Sometimes the true cause has little to do with outdated finishes and much more to do with structural relationships, mechanical systems, or how different areas of the home interact with one another.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For example, a homeowner may believe that a kitchen feels too small when the real issue is poor circulation caused by unnecessary walls or awkward appliance placement. Another family may request a larger bathroom because storage feels limited, only to discover that reorganizing adjacent space provides the same benefit without expanding the footprint. These opportunities become visible only after evaluating the house as a complete system rather than focusing on a single room. Harris &amp; Sons regularly finds solutions that improve daily living while avoiding unnecessary construction costs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This broader approach also helps prioritize investments. Instead of allocating the majority of the budget toward cosmetic upgrades, homeowners gain a clearer understanding of where improvements will have the greatest long-term impact. Structural reinforcement, insulation upgrades, ventilation improvements, and electrical modernization may not be immediately visible, but they often provide far greater value than decorative finishes alone. Harris &amp; Sons helps clients make these decisions with confidence by presenting the complete picture before construction begins.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Looking Beyond the Room You Plan to Remodel<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every room in a house influences the spaces around it. Remodeling one area without understanding those relationships can create inconsistencies in function, appearance, or performance. Harris &amp; Sons evaluates how each room connects with neighboring spaces, ensuring that improvements strengthen the home as a whole rather than creating isolated upgrades. This comprehensive planning results in renovations that feel cohesive instead of fragmented.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Kitchen renovations provide a good example. Updating cabinets and countertops may improve aesthetics, but if adjacent dining areas remain disconnected or traffic patterns remain inefficient, the renovation may still fall short of homeowner expectations. Harris &amp; Sons studies how family members move throughout the home before recommending layout changes. Improving these connections often creates a greater sense of openness without increasing square footage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bathrooms present similar opportunities. Poor ventilation, aging plumbing, or moisture concerns may originate outside the room itself. Addressing only surface materials without investigating the surrounding systems can allow hidden problems to persist. Harris &amp; Sons examines these underlying conditions before recommending finishes, ensuring that every completed renovation performs as well as it looks.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.epa.gov\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)<\/a><\/strong> emphasizes that indoor environmental quality depends on proper moisture control, ventilation, and healthy building practices rather than appearance alone. Harris &amp; Sons integrates these principles into every whole home evaluation so homeowners receive improvements that contribute to both comfort and long-term durability. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/smiling-architect-and-general-contractor-shaking-h-2023-11-27-05-17-06-utc-1024x683-1.webp\" alt=\"whole home evaluation before remodeling consultation\" class=\"wp-image-6201\" srcset=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/smiling-architect-and-general-contractor-shaking-h-2023-11-27-05-17-06-utc-1024x683-1.webp 1024w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/smiling-architect-and-general-contractor-shaking-h-2023-11-27-05-17-06-utc-1024x683-1-300x200.webp 300w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/smiling-architect-and-general-contractor-shaking-h-2023-11-27-05-17-06-utc-1024x683-1-768x512.webp 768w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/smiling-architect-and-general-contractor-shaking-h-2023-11-27-05-17-06-utc-1024x683-1-600x400.webp 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Understanding How Systems Work Together<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Behind every finished wall is a network of systems that quietly support everyday life. Electrical wiring powers appliances, plumbing delivers clean water, HVAC equipment regulates comfort, insulation controls energy performance, and structural framing supports the entire building. None of these systems operate independently. A change in one area often influences several others, making coordination essential during any renovation. Harris &amp; Sons approaches remodeling with this interconnected mindset from the very beginning.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">During a whole home evaluation, the team carefully examines how these systems interact before any demolition begins. Relocating plumbing fixtures may affect framing. Removing a wall could change HVAC duct routing. Adding larger windows might require structural modifications while also influencing insulation and energy efficiency. By identifying these relationships early, Harris &amp; Sons develops renovation plans that integrate every system instead of forcing adjustments later during construction.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This level of planning minimizes costly delays while improving the overall quality of the finished project. Contractors working without a comprehensive evaluation often encounter unexpected obstacles after demolition begins, leading to schedule changes and additional expenses. Harris &amp; Sons believes homeowners deserve greater certainty before construction starts. Their evaluation process significantly reduces surprises by revealing potential challenges while solutions are still easy to implement.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.iccsafe.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">International Code Council (ICC)<\/a><\/strong> provides nationally recognized standards that guide safe structural modifications, mechanical coordination, and residential construction practices. Harris &amp; Sons follows these established guidelines throughout every project, ensuring that renovation plans not only meet design goals but also satisfy modern building requirements.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Preventing Expensive Surprises Before Construction Begins<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One of the greatest advantages of a whole home evaluation is its ability to uncover hidden issues before they become expensive problems. Older homes often contain aging wiring, outdated plumbing, moisture damage, settling foundations, or structural modifications completed decades earlier under different building standards. Many of these conditions remain invisible until demolition begins. Discovering them after construction is underway frequently results in budget increases, scheduling delays, and difficult decisions for homeowners.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Harris &amp; Sons believes these surprises should be minimized whenever possible. Their evaluation process includes careful investigation of accessible structural components, existing mechanical systems, moisture-prone areas, and previous renovation work. Rather than treating these discoveries as unexpected obstacles, they incorporate solutions into the original project plan whenever feasible. This proactive approach allows homeowners to make informed decisions before committing to construction.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Planning ahead also creates more accurate project timelines. When hidden conditions are identified early, materials can be ordered appropriately, subcontractors can be scheduled more efficiently, and construction sequencing becomes far more predictable. Homeowners benefit from fewer interruptions and greater confidence throughout the renovation process. Harris &amp; Sons views this preparation as one of the most valuable services they provide because it protects both the client&#8217;s investment and overall experience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why a Whole Home Evaluation Leads to Smarter Budget Planning<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A remodeling budget is one of the first topics homeowners want to discuss, yet it is also one of the hardest to estimate accurately without understanding the property&#8217;s overall condition. Many renovation budgets increase not because the original estimate was unrealistic, but because important issues were discovered only after construction had already begun. Hidden plumbing concerns, structural deficiencies, outdated electrical systems, or moisture damage can quickly change the scope of work. Harris &amp; Sons minimizes these surprises by making the whole home evaluation the foundation of every remodeling plan, allowing clients to make financial decisions based on reliable information instead of assumptions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This approach also helps homeowners prioritize their investment more effectively. During the evaluation, Harris &amp; Sons distinguishes between improvements that are essential for safety and long-term performance and those that are primarily cosmetic. Clients can clearly see where their budget will create the greatest value. In many cases, modest adjustments to infrastructure, storage, or circulation provide more meaningful improvements than expensive decorative upgrades. By explaining these options in detail, Harris &amp; Sons empowers homeowners to invest with confidence rather than feeling pressured to spend more than necessary.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Budget planning also becomes more flexible when the entire home has been evaluated. Some homeowners choose to complete their renovation in phases, addressing the highest-priority improvements first while preparing for future projects. Because Harris &amp; Sons develops a comprehensive understanding of the property from the beginning, every phase can be planned to support the next. This prevents duplicate work, protects completed areas, and ensures that future improvements integrate seamlessly with earlier renovations. Thoughtful planning today often saves considerable time and money later.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">A Harris &amp; Sons Project Example: Solving More Than the Original Problem<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One Harris &amp; Sons project began with what seemed like a straightforward request to remodel an aging kitchen. The homeowners wanted updated cabinetry, new countertops, improved lighting, and a more contemporary appearance. During the initial conversation, however, the design team noticed that the kitchen&#8217;s challenges extended well beyond outdated finishes. Family members constantly crossed through the cooking area to reach other parts of the house, storage was scattered across several rooms, and natural light struggled to reach the center of the floor plan. These issues suggested that appearance alone would not solve the underlying problems.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As part of the whole home evaluation, Harris &amp; Sons examined the surrounding spaces, structural framing, utility locations, and circulation throughout the main level. They discovered that a small hallway and an underused pantry were creating unnecessary congestion while limiting opportunities for better storage. Instead of recommending a costly addition, the team redesigned the relationship between the kitchen, dining area, and adjacent living space. This created a more intuitive layout that improved movement, increased storage capacity, and allowed daylight to travel more naturally throughout the home.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The evaluation also uncovered aging electrical wiring and insulation that no longer met modern expectations. Since walls would already be opened during construction, Harris &amp; Sons recommended upgrading these systems at the same time. Although these improvements remained hidden after completion, they enhanced energy efficiency, improved safety, and reduced the likelihood of future repairs. The homeowners appreciated knowing these concerns had been addressed before they developed into larger issues.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When the project was finished, visitors immediately noticed the beautiful kitchen, but the homeowners valued something even greater. Everyday routines became easier, family gatherings felt more comfortable, and the entire main level functioned more naturally. What started as a kitchen renovation ultimately improved the experience of living throughout the entire home. This project perfectly illustrates why Harris &amp; Sons believes that successful remodeling begins with understanding the whole property rather than focusing on one room alone.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"577\" src=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-1024x577.png\" alt=\"whole home evaluation creating connected living spaces through Harris &amp; Sons remodeling\" class=\"wp-image-13250\" srcset=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-1024x577.png 1024w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-300x169.png 300w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-768x433.png 768w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-1536x865.png 1536w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-2048x1154.png 2048w, https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/Ruby_peak_1-1-600x338.png 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Long-Term Benefits of a Whole Home Evaluation<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The greatest value of a whole home evaluation often becomes apparent long after construction has been completed. While new finishes naturally attract attention immediately, the underlying planning continues providing benefits every day. Homes designed with a complete understanding of their structure, systems, and daily use typically require fewer corrective repairs, operate more efficiently, and adapt more easily as families&#8217; needs evolve. Harris &amp; Sons views these long-term advantages as one of the strongest reasons to begin every remodeling project with a comprehensive assessment rather than a narrow focus on individual rooms.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A complete evaluation also strengthens the home&#8217;s overall durability. When structural components, insulation, ventilation, moisture protection, plumbing, and electrical systems are considered together, each improvement supports the others. Instead of addressing isolated issues, Harris &amp; Sons creates balanced renovations where every element contributes to the home&#8217;s overall performance. This integrated approach helps reduce maintenance costs while improving comfort throughout every season of the year.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Future remodeling projects become easier as well. Because Harris &amp; Sons documents the property&#8217;s existing conditions and develops a long-range understanding of its systems, homeowners have a valuable roadmap for future improvements. Whether they decide to remodel another room several years later or expand the house altogether, previous work can be incorporated efficiently without unnecessary demolition or redesign. A carefully planned renovation creates opportunities rather than limitations.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.usa.gov\/agencies\/u-s-department-of-housing-and-urban-development\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD)<\/a><\/strong> encourages homeowners to protect long-term property value through preventive maintenance, careful planning, and quality construction practices. Harris &amp; Sons shares this philosophy by approaching every project with the understanding that today&#8217;s decisions influence the home&#8217;s performance for decades to come.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Harris &amp; Sons Makes Evaluation the First Step<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every remodeling company has its own process, but Harris &amp; Sons has built its reputation on careful preparation before construction begins. Rather than rushing into design concepts or material selections, their team first develops a thorough understanding of the property and the people who live there. This includes discussing lifestyle, future goals, existing challenges, and long-term expectations while also evaluating the home&#8217;s structural and mechanical condition. These conversations allow every recommendation to be based on evidence instead of assumptions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The evaluation process is collaborative rather than technical for the sake of complexity. Harris &amp; Sons believes homeowners should understand why each recommendation is being made and how it contributes to the success of the overall project. Clients are encouraged to ask questions, explore alternatives, and participate in important decisions from the earliest planning stages. This open communication creates trust while ensuring that every renovation reflects the homeowner&#8217;s priorities as well as professional construction expertise.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By beginning with a whole home evaluation, Harris &amp; Sons creates renovation plans that are realistic, coordinated, and designed for lasting performance. Construction proceeds more smoothly because important decisions have already been made thoughtfully rather than reactively. Budgets become more reliable, schedules become more predictable, and homeowners gain confidence knowing their investment has been carefully planned before work begins.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This commitment to preparation distinguishes Harris &amp; Sons from contractors who focus only on the immediate scope of work. They understand that remodeling is not simply about changing a room; it is about improving how the entire home functions. That philosophy continues to guide every project they undertake, regardless of size or complexity.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Conclusion: Great Renovations Begin with Understanding the Entire Home<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Successful remodeling is rarely the result of good design alone. It begins with understanding how a home functions as a complete system and identifying the opportunities that may not be immediately visible. A whole home evaluation provides that understanding by revealing how structure, mechanical systems, natural light, circulation, storage, and everyday living patterns work together. Instead of solving one isolated problem, it creates the opportunity to improve the entire living experience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Harris &amp; Sons has made this philosophy the foundation of their remodeling process. Every project starts with careful observation, thoughtful discussion, and detailed evaluation before design decisions are finalized. This approach allows the team to anticipate challenges, identify opportunities, and recommend improvements that create lasting value rather than temporary solutions. It also provides homeowners with greater confidence because every recommendation is supported by a comprehensive understanding of the property.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The benefits extend well beyond construction. Homes that are planned holistically tend to perform more efficiently, require fewer unexpected repairs, adapt more easily to changing lifestyles, and maintain their value over time. These outcomes are rarely achieved by focusing on finishes alone. They are the result of careful preparation, professional expertise, and a willingness to look beyond what is immediately visible. Harris &amp; Sons believes these are the qualities that separate ordinary renovations from truly exceptional remodeling projects.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you are considering updating your home, begin by asking a different question. Instead of deciding what room should change first, ask how your entire home could work better for the people who live there. Harris &amp; Sons is ready to guide that conversation through a comprehensive whole home evaluation, helping you build a renovation plan that is practical, thoughtful, and designed to deliver value for many years to come.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">External Links<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.epa.gov\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)<\/a><\/strong> <\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.iccsafe.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">International Code Council (ICC)<\/a><\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.usa.gov\/agencies\/u-s-department-of-housing-and-urban-development\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD)<\/strong> <\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Internal Links<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/about-us\/\"><strong>Harris &amp; Sons- About Us<\/strong><\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/services\/\">Our Services<\/a><\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us\/\">Contact Us<\/a><\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Most homeowners begin planning a renovation with a single room in mind. It might be an outdated kitchen, a bathroom that no longer meets the family&#8217;s needs, or a living area that feels disconnected from the rest of the house. While focusing on one space is completely natural, it can sometimes limit the overall success [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":13250,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-16403","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/16403","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=16403"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/16403\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":16404,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/16403\/revisions\/16404"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/13250"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=16403"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=16403"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=16403"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}